{"ts": "2026-11-02T16:09:00.447167Z", "run_id": "r-20261102T1606Z-fa14", "unit": "openspec:add-web-flow-graph", "seq": 14, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-007", "id": "Q-007", "status": "answered", "reason": "layout-rf1.test.ts builds RF1_LAYOUT and G_LAYOUT from the reference figures (RF-1: width 384, height 912, 9 layers, 11 nodes, 12 edges; G: 384 by 288, 3 layers) and deep-equals them with layoutFlow on the catalogue flow, its canonicalisation and both parsed texts, then asserts validateFlow ok for GRAPH_GOOD and one L2_UNKNOWN_BLOCK at /nodes/fetch/uses for GRAPH_BAD. layout.ts implements the geometry rules of design decision 2. Exact coordinates cannot be read from a page, so an e2e test is not applicable.", "called": true, "tasks": [], "target": "H-afa2b3ee", "kind": "verdict", "batch": "Q-006+5", "batch_size": 5, "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.383976, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "303ba1430f3a19adf56ef41ae02db8586384a7468ea15cb27946867773f041d8", "checked": [{"ref": "test/web-flow-graph/layout-rf1.test.ts:181", "quote": "test(\"C-1129d3e7 RF-1 and the journey flow have fixed coordinates\", () => {", "claim": "A Node test traces the criterion."}, {"ref": "test/web-flow-graph/layout-rf1.test.ts:183", "quote": "assert.deepEqual(layoutOf(flow, \"RF-1\"), RF1_LAYOUT);", "claim": "The RF-1 layout is deep-compared with the fixed figures."}, {"ref": "test/web-flow-graph/layout-rf1.test.ts:202", "quote": "assert.equal(issue.code, \"L2_UNKNOWN_BLOCK\");", "claim": "The validator result for GRAPH_BAD is asserted to be the single L2_UNKNOWN_BLOCK error."}, {"ref": "web/src/flow-graph/layout.ts:302", "quote": "x: GRAPH_GEOMETRY.margin + (maxCount - list.length) * 96 + index * 192,", "claim": "The implementation computes coordinates by the fixed geometry rule of the design."}, {"ref": "e2e/test_m3_authoring.py:83", "quote": "expect(graph).to_contain_text(\"Flow graph: 4 nodes, 3 edges, 3 layers.\")", "claim": "The browser journey already shows the G layout's node, edge and layer counts on the page."}]}
